@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g3-licensee-duties.l4: Chapter 3 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025, sections 12 to 16: the duties a licensee owes.
-- Written by ENCODER G3.  Imports only prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain.
--
-- What this module decides:
--   s.12  a licence is personal: no transfer, no permission for another person to use it (SHANT).
--   s.13  work is done to parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994, in the wording from time to time (SHANT of
--         the converse; compliance with the Standard is an INPUT, the Standard is not in the sources).
--         The one violation the Third Schedule prices for s.13 (item (4)) is a separate, narrower decision.
--   s.14  the orderer of the work may demand to see the licence; the licensee must show it (MAY, then MUST).
--   s.15  the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents; the licensee must supply them.
--   s.16  the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars within 30 days.
--
-- Inputs taken from other groups, under the standard names of PLAN section (c):
--   `licence kinds in force on the day` (IP1, G2/G1), `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` (IP2, G7),
--   `the act is work on a cooling system` (IP4, G1).  The Calendar of rest days is IP15.
--   Fork COM: s.63(a) fixes commencement only "for the performance of work on a system".  Ss.13 and 14 concern such work and the input fits them.
--   Ss.12, 15 and 16 concern a licensee and not one piece of work: the input is read there as "the Law has commenced for the licensee's work",
--   which the sources do not decide (trap T20); passing TRUE gives the reading with no commencement gate.
--   Every opinion of the Registrar is an input named `in the Registrar's opinion ...` (IP17).
--
-- THE UNIT OF EVERY WITHIN IN THIS MODULE IS DAYS, and only this comment says so: the clock of a #TRACE
-- starts at 0 on the day the duty arises, and a WITHIN of n means the n-th day counted by IL s.10(a).
--
-- Interpretation Law s.10 counts forwards only.  The one period of this module that it counts is the 30 days
-- of s.16 (kind D: a deadline for doing something).  The brief's ruling 4 applies IL s.10(c) to a kind D, so the
-- reading taken moves the last day off a day of rest; the reading without IL s.10(c) is `s.16 — the last day for notifying the
-- Registrar, counting only IL s.10(a), of a change made on` below.  The time of s.15 is a day the Registrar directs (kind X, an input date, never counted).
-- The rules of section 17 count a year backwards and are in g3-training-duty.l4.
--
-- Forks and what the sources do not answer are in FRAGMENT-G3.md; the fork numbers in comments are its.

§ `Chapter 3: Duties and restrictions on a licensee and an operator, sections 12 to 16`

-- src:127 | {{ח:קטע2|פרק ג|פרק ג׳: חובות והגבלות על בעל רישיון ומפעיל}}

§§ `Nouns of sections 12 to 16`

-- The acts that sections 12 to 16 speak of, named by what is done and not by the section; the party that
-- does each is the `Party` of the rule that uses it.
@ref s.12 to s.16 (src:130-142)
DECLARE `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law` IS ONE OF
    `transfer the licence to another person` HAS `the person to whom the licence is transferred` IS A Person
    `permit another person to use the licence` HAS `the person permitted to use the licence` IS A Person
    `perform work on a cooling system`
    `demand to see the licence`
    `show the licence to the orderer of the work`
    `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents`
    `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required`
    `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars`

-- A wording of Israeli Standard 994 and what the work was found to be against it.
-- The Standard is outside the sources (T13): conformity is the finding of whoever tested the work, an input.
-- Each wording carries the day it took effect, because s.13 takes the Standard "as its wording is from time to time" (fork S13a).
@ref s.13 (src:133)
DECLARE `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` HAS
    `the day this wording took effect` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which this wording of the Standard was in force
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The finding that the work conformed to part 4 of the Standard as worded on the day it took effect
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The finding that the tightness test the testing chapter of part 4 requires was performed
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The finding that the work conformed to part 5 of the Standard as worded on the day it took effect

-- The kinds of demand section 15 gives the Registrar.
@ref s.15 (src:139)
DECLARE `Kind of demand under section 15` IS ONE OF
    `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law`

-- The Registrar's demand of section 15, as facts and as the Registrar's opinions (IP17).
@ref s.15 (src:139)
DECLARE `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` HAS
    `the kind of demand` IS A `Kind of demand under section 15` @desc Whether the Registrar demands a report or demands information or documents
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a report: the particulars are in connection with the licensee's engagement as a licensee
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For information or documents: the Registrar's opinion that they are needed to realise the purposes of the Law
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar made the supply a condition for renewal or extension of the licence
    `the day of the demand` IS A DATE @desc The day the demand was made to the licensee
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day for compliance that the Registrar directed; NOTHING if the Registrar directed none

-- A demand by the orderer of the work to see the licence (section 14).
@ref s.14 (src:136)
DECLARE `Demand to see the licence` HAS
    `the person demanding ordered the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person demanding is the orderer of the work on the cooling system
    `the person demanded to see the licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the orderer demanded to see the licence
    `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licensee did not show the licence when the demand was made (when failure begins is not stated in section 14, fork S14)

-- A change in the particulars given in a licence application (section 16).
@ref s.16 (src:142)
DECLARE `Change in the application particulars` HAS
    `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the particular that changed was among those the licensee gave in the application for the licence
    `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the particular changed; IL s.10(a) does not count it
    `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar directed the manner in which a change is to be notified
    `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice followed the directed manner; read only when the Registrar directed one
    `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day the licensee gave notice of the change to the Registrar; NOTHING if no notice has been given (whether the day is that of dispatch or of receipt the sources do not say)

§§ `Named refusals of sections 12 to 16`

-- A refusal is returned in the position of the answer, never stored (an unforced REFUSE is no refusal); its name is its message.

@ref s.13 (src:133)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s.13 — no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "s.13: no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied, so conformity to parts 4 and 5 cannot be answered"

@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s.15 — the day the Registrar directed for compliance precedes the day of the demand` MEANS
    REFUSE "s.15: the day the Registrar directed for compliance precedes the day of the demand, so no period can be counted"

§§ `The licensee`

-- The persons these sections bind are "holders of a licence" (s.2): a person with a licence in force on the day.
-- IP1 supplies the kinds in force; the licensee is a person with at least one.
-- src:43 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בעל רישיון“ – בעל רישיון לבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר לפי הוראות חוק זה;
@ref s.2 "licensee" (src:43)
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day` MEANS
    NOT (null `licence kinds in force on the day`)

§§ `12. Prohibition on transferring a licence`

-- src:129 | {{ח:סעיף|12|איסור העברת רישיון}}
-- src:130 | {{ח:ת}} רישיון הוא אישי; בעל רישיון לא יעביר את הרישיון שבידו לאדם אחר ולא יתיר לאדם אחר לעשות שימוש ברישיונו.
@ref s.12 (src:129-130)
GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence
      `the other person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.12 — the person is another person than the holder of the licence` `the licence` `the other person` MEANS
    NOT (`the other person`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS `the licence`'s `the holder`'s `reference for the person`)

@ref s.12 (src:130)
@export Decides whether a licensee's transfer of the licence to another person is contrary to section 12 of the Law, which makes a licence personal
GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
      `the other person` IS A Person @desc The person to whom the licence is transferred, or whom the licensee permits to use it
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `the licence` `the other person` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND `s.12 — the person is another person than the holder of the licence` `the licence` `the other person`

@ref s.12 (src:130)
GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence
      `the other person` IS A Person
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `the licence` `the other person` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND `s.12 — the person is another person than the holder of the licence` `the licence` `the other person`

-- "Shall not transfer ... and shall not permit": two prohibitions, both standing for as long as the person holds the licence,
-- so neither carries a WITHIN (a SHANT with a WITHIN sunsets at it).  The guard says what "another person" is.
@ref s.12 (src:130)
GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.12 — the licensee shall not transfer the licence or permit another person to use it` `the licence` MEANS
        (PARTY `the licensee`
         SHANT `transfer the licence to another person` recipient
               PROVIDED `s.12 — the person is another person than the holder of the licence` `the licence` recipient
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the licensee` BECAUSE "s.12: the licensee transferred the licence to another person")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the licensee`
         SHANT `permit another person to use the licence` user
               PROVIDED `s.12 — the person is another person than the holder of the licence` `the licence` user
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the licensee` BECAUSE "s.12: the licensee permitted another person to use the licence")

§§ `13. Duty to meet the Standard`

-- src:132 | {{ח:סעיף|13|חובת עמידה בתקן}}
-- src:133 | {{ח:ת}} בעל רישיון יבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר המנויה {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|בתוספת הראשונה}} בהתאם לחלקים 4 ו־5 לתקן ישראלי ת״י 994, כפי נוסחם מזמן לזמן.
@ref s.13 (src:132-133)
GIVEN `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.13 — section 13 applies to the work` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`

-- "As their wording is from time to time" (fork S13a): the wording that counts is the latest one in force on the day the work
-- is judged against.  Several wordings may be supplied; none in force on that day is a named refusal.
@ref s.13 (src:133)
GIVEN wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`s.13 — the latest of the wordings` wordings MEANS
    CONSIDER wordings
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN w FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `s.13 — the latest of the wordings` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST w
        WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (IF r's `the day this wording took effect` GREATER THAN w's `the day this wording took effect` THEN r ELSE w)

@ref s.13 (src:133)
GIVEN `the day the work is judged against` IS A DATE
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`s.13 — the wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on` `the day the work is judged against` wordings MEANS
    `s.13 — the latest of the wordings`
        (filter (GIVEN w YIELD w's `the day this wording took effect` AT MOST `the day the work is judged against`) wordings)

@ref s.13 (src:133)
GIVEN `the day the work is judged against` IS A DATE
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.13 — the work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of the wording in force on` `the day the work is judged against` wordings MEANS
    CONSIDER `s.13 — the wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on` `the day the work is judged against` wordings
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s.13 — no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied`
    WHEN JUST w THEN w's `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` AND w's `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording`

-- The reading taken (S13a): the work is judged against the wording in force on the day the work was done.
@ref s.13 (src:133)
@export Decides whether a licensee breached section 13, by doing work on a cooling system otherwise than in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994 in the wording in force on the day of the work
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item` @desc The piece of work: who did it, whether it was installation or maintenance, on which system, and on which day
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` @desc The wordings of Israeli Standard 994 against which the work was judged, each with the day it took effect and the findings on the work
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system, an act of a kind the First Schedule lists (decided by the licensing group)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
        `s.13 — section 13 applies to the work` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND NOT `s.13 — the work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of the wording in force on` (`the work`'s `date performed`) wordings

-- The alternative reading (S13a): the work is judged against the wording in force on the day it is inspected.
@ref s.13 (src:133)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item`
      `the day of the inspection` IS A DATE
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.13 — the licensee breached section 13, judged against the wording in force on the day of the inspection` `the work` `the day of the inspection` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
        `s.13 — section 13 applies to the work` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND NOT `s.13 — the work conformed to parts 4 and 5 of the wording in force on` `the day of the inspection` wordings

-- "Shall perform ... in accordance with": a constraint on HOW work is done, not a duty to do work, so it is a prohibition of the converse
-- (fork S13b).  It carries no WITHIN: it holds while the person is a licensee.
@ref s.13 (src:132-133)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item`
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.13 — the licensee shall do the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    PARTY `the licensee`
    SHANT `perform work on a cooling system`
          PROVIDED `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the licensee` BECAUSE "s.13: the work was not done in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994 in the wording in force on the day of the work"

-- Alternative S13b: the text's own form, a MUST, with no deadline because none is stated.  The act that discharges it is work done in
-- accordance with the Standard (the guard); work not in accordance does not match the act, and since no deadline runs, no breach can ever be traced.
@ref s.13 (src:132-133)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item`
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.13 — the licensee must perform the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994, in the text's own form` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    PARTY `the licensee`
    MUST `perform work on a cooling system`
         PROVIDED NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The Third Schedule prices ONE failure under s.13, item (4): "a licensee who performed an installation of a cooling system without
-- performing a tightness test of the refrigerant piping in accordance with the testing chapter of part 4 of Israeli Standard 994".
-- Other breaches of s.13 are breaches with no row (T13).  NOTHING here means "no Third Schedule row", NOT "no breach".
-- src:715 | {{ח:תת|(4)}} בעל רישיון שביצע התקנה של מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי לבצע בדיקת אטימות לצנרת חומר הקירור בהתאם להוראות הקבועות בפרק הבדיקות בתקן ישראלי ת״י 994 חלק 4 – מזגני אוויר: התקנה, בניגוד להוראת {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 13|סעיף 13}};
@ref s.13 (src:133); Third Schedule item (4) (src:715)
@export Returns the Third Schedule violation committed under section 13 (an installation without the tightness test of the refrigerant piping), or nothing when no Third Schedule item prices the breach
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item` @desc The piece of work: who did it, whether it was installation or maintenance, on which system, and on which day
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` @desc The wordings of Israeli Standard 994 against which the work was judged, each with the day it took effect and the findings on the work
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system, an act of a kind the First Schedule lists (decided by the licensing group)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    IF       `s.13 — section 13 applies to the work` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
         AND `the work`'s `the kind of job` EQUALS `an installation job`
         AND NOT `s.13 — the tightness test was performed under the wording in force on` (`the work`'s `date performed`) wordings
    THEN JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s.13 (src:133); Third Schedule item (4) (src:715)
GIVEN `the day the work is judged against` IS A DATE
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.13 — the tightness test was performed under the wording in force on` `the day the work is judged against` wordings MEANS
    CONSIDER `s.13 — the wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on` `the day the work is judged against` wordings
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s.13 — no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied`
    WHEN JUST w THEN w's `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires`

-- Alternative S13c: item (4) names the testing chapter of part 4 under the Standard's TITLE as enacted ("Air conditioners: installation"), while s.13
-- follows the Standard "from time to time".  Read item (4) as frozen to the wording in force on a fixed day (the day the Law was published, an input),
-- the tightness test is judged against that wording whatever wording governs s.13.
@ref s.13 (src:133); Third Schedule item (4) (src:715)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item`
      `the day whose wording fixes the testing chapter` IS A DATE
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13, the testing chapter being that of the wording in force on a fixed day` `the work` `the day whose wording fixes the testing chapter` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    IF       `s.13 — section 13 applies to the work` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
         AND `the work`'s `the kind of job` EQUALS `an installation job`
         AND NOT `s.13 — the tightness test was performed under the wording in force on` `the day whose wording fixes the testing chapter` wordings
    THEN JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The record Chapter 6 takes (IP9): the licensee, the listed violation, a reference for the act, the day of the act.
@ref s.13 (src:133); Third Schedule item (4) (src:715)
@export Returns the violation record for Chapter 6 when a licensee installed a cooling system without the tightness test of part 4 of Israeli Standard 994, or nothing
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Work item` @desc The piece of work: who did it, whether it was installation or maintenance, on which system, and on which day
      `reference for the act` IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies the act; two violations with the same reference are one act
      wordings IS A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` @desc The wordings of Israeli Standard 994 against which the work was judged, each with the day it took effect and the findings on the work
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system, an act of a kind the First Schedule lists (decided by the licensing group)
GIVETH A MAYBE Violation
`s.13 — the violation committed under section 13` `the work` `reference for the act` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `the work` wordings `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST listed THEN JUST (Violation WITH
        `the violator` IS `the work`'s `performed by`
        `the listed violation` IS listed
        `reference for the act` IS `reference for the act`
        `date of the act` IS `the work`'s `date performed`)

§§ `14. Duty to show the licence`

-- src:135 | {{ח:סעיף|14|חובת הצגת רישיון}}
-- src:136 | {{ח:ת}} בעל רישיון יציג את רישיונו למזמין עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר, לפי דרישתו.
@ref s.14 (src:135-136)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand to see the licence`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` demand `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND demand's `the person demanding ordered the work`
    AND demand's `the person demanded to see the licence`

@ref s.14 (src:136)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand to see the licence`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` demand `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` demand `the act is work on a cooling system` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND demand's `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand`

-- "On his demand": the licensee's duty arises with the demand and has no time stated, so it carries no WITHIN (fork S14).
-- Nothing is owed before the demand, and an orderer who never demands has used a liberty (MAY), not failed in a duty.
@ref s.14 (src:136)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.14 — the orderer of the work may demand to see the licence, and the licensee must then show it` MEANS
    PARTY `the orderer of the work`
    MAY `demand to see the licence`
    HENCE (PARTY `the licensee`
           MUST `show the licence to the orderer of the work`
           HENCE FULFILLED)

§§ `15. Duty to report to the Registrar`

-- src:138 | {{ח:סעיף|15|חובת דיווח לרשם}}
-- src:139 | {{ח:ת}} הרשם רשאי לדרוש מבעל רישיון לדווח לו על פרטים בקשר לעיסוקו כבעל רישיון, כפי שהורה, ולמסור לו כל מידע או מסמכים הדרושים לו לשם מימוש מטרות חוק זה, לרבות כתנאי לחידוש או להארכה של רישיון, ובעל הרישיון ימסור לו את המידע או המסמכים כאמור.
@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.15 — the demand keeps within the limit of its kind` demand MEANS
    CONSIDER demand's `the kind of demand`
    WHEN `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee` THEN demand's `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    WHEN `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law` THEN demand's `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law`

@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND `s.15 — the demand keeps within the limit of its kind` demand

-- "As he directed": the Registrar may direct the day by which the report or supply is made (kind X: a day an official fixes,
-- an input, never counted).  No direction is no time limit: the text states none (fork S15).
@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` demand MEANS
    CONSIDER demand's `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST directed THEN
        IF Day directed AT LEAST Day (demand's `the day of the demand`)
        THEN JUST (Day directed MINUS Day (demand's `the day of the demand`))
        ELSE `s.15 — the day the Registrar directed for compliance precedes the day of the demand`

@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.15 — the licensee must report or supply what the Registrar demanded` demand MEANS
    CONSIDER `s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` demand
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        PARTY `the licensee`
        MUST `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    WHEN JUST days THEN
        PARTY `the licensee`
        MUST `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required`
        WITHIN days
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the licensee` BECAUSE "s.15: the licensee did not report or supply what the Registrar demanded by the day the Registrar directed"

@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
    IF   `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents`
         HENCE `s.15 — the licensee must report or supply what the Registrar demanded` demand
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The licensee's duty to comply.  The last clause of s.15 says "the licensee shall supply to him the INFORMATION OR DOCUMENTS as stated"; it does
-- not repeat the REPORT.  Taken (fork S15b): the duty reaches both limbs, since a power to demand a report that bound nobody would be empty.
-- Alternative S15b: only what the clause names, so a demand for a report creates no duty of the licensee.
@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
    `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`

@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand, the express duty reaching only information or documents` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` demand `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND demand's `the kind of demand` EQUALS `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law`

-- "Including as a condition for renewal or extension": a demand made on that footing is a condition the licence
-- cannot be renewed or extended without.  G2 (s.8) and G1 (s.10(a)) consume this as an input.
@ref s.15 (src:139)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
      `the licensee reported or supplied what the Registrar demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.15 — the condition for renewing or extending the licence is satisfied` demand `the licensee reported or supplied what the Registrar demanded` MEANS
    (NOT demand's `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence`)
    OR `the licensee reported or supplied what the Registrar demanded`

§§ `16. Duty to update particulars`

-- src:141 | {{ח:סעיף|16|חובת עדכון פרטים}}
-- src:142 | {{ח:ת}} בעל רישיון יודיע לרשם על כל שינוי בפרטים שמסר בבקשה לרישיון, באופן שעליו יורה הרשם, בתוך 30 ימים מיום השינוי.

-- IL s.10(a): the 30 days run from the day of the change and the day of the change is not counted, so the days are D+1 to D+30.
-- Reading taken (fork S16, kind D): IL s.10(c) applies, so a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday moves to the
-- first later day that is not one.  The calendar is IP15, an input; no holiday is computed.
@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` `the day of the change` `the calendar` MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` `the day of the change` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (`the calendar`'s `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

-- The alternative (fork S16): IL s.10(a) alone, the last day being the thirtieth day whatever it is.
@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar, counting only IL s.10(a), of a change made on` `the day of the change` MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` `the day of the change`

-- The number of days the licensee has, counted from the day of the change: the WITHIN of the rule below.
@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s.16 — the number of days allowed for notifying a change made on` `the day of the change` `the calendar` MEANS
    Day (`s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` `the day of the change` `the calendar`) MINUS Day `the day of the change`

-- A notice counts only if it was given and, where the Registrar directed a manner, it followed the manner.
@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN change IS A `Change in the application particulars`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.16 — the notice counts as given` change MEANS
    CONSIDER change's `the day the notice was given to the Registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN (NOT change's `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying`) OR change's `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed`

@ref s.16 (src:142)
@export Decides whether a licensee gave the Registrar valid notice of a change in the particulars of the licence application within 30 days from the day of the change, counted under Interpretation Law section 10(a) and (c)
GIVEN change IS A `Change in the application particulars` @desc The change in the particulars given in the licence application, and the notice of it if any
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under any enactment, for the years the question touches; a list that runs out answers not a rest day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` change `the calendar` MEANS
    CONSIDER change's `the day the notice was given to the Registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN
            change's `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application`
        AND `s.16 — the notice counts as given` change
        AND given AT MOST `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (change's `the day of the change`) `the calendar`

@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN change IS A `Change in the application particulars`
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.16 — the notice was given after the last day` change `the calendar` MEANS
    CONSIDER change's `the day the notice was given to the Registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN given GREATER THAN `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (change's `the day of the change`) `the calendar`

-- Breach is a question about a day: before the last day a missing notice is a notice not yet due.
@ref s.16 (src:142)
@export Decides whether, on a given day, a licensee has breached the duty of section 16 to notify the Registrar of a change within 30 days
GIVEN `the day the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is put; a deadline is not breached before its last day has passed
      change IS A `Change in the application particulars` @desc The change in the particulars given in the licence application, and the notice of it if any
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under any enactment, for the years the question touches; a list that runs out answers not a rest day
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The licence kinds in force on the day of the act, from the licence group; an empty list if none is in force
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced for the work on the system, under section 63 (decided by the commencement group)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` `the day the question is asked` change `the calendar` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
        `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
    AND change's `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application`
    AND (IF   `s.16 — the notice counts as given` change
         THEN `s.16 — the notice was given after the last day` change `the calendar`
         ELSE `the day the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (change's `the day of the change`) `the calendar`)

@ref s.16 (src:142)
GIVEN change IS A `Change in the application particulars`
      `the calendar` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 12 to 16 of the Law`
`s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` change `the calendar` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a licensee on the day, for sections 12 to 16` `licence kinds in force on the day`
         AND `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
         AND change's `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application`
    THEN PARTY `the licensee`
         MUST `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars`
              PROVIDED (NOT change's `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying`) OR change's `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed`
         WITHIN `s.16 — the number of days allowed for notifying a change made on` (change's `the day of the change`) `the calendar`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the licensee` BECAUSE "s.16: the licensee did not notify the Registrar of the change in the particulars given in the licence application within 30 days from the day of the change (IL s.10(a), (c))"
    ELSE FULFILLED
